    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d73">

                <pb facs="0131" n="49" sameAs="frus:frus1945Malta/pg49"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">
                    UNA Files</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Stettinius</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the President
                    </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d73-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1944-11-15">November 15, 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Memorandum for the President</hi>
                </p>
                <p rendition="#flush">Subject: Questions Left Unsettled at Dumbarton Oaks</p>
                <p>There are six principal questions which need to be settled in connection with the
                    establishment of the United Nations organization. They are as follows: <list>
                        <label>1.</label>
                        <item>Voting procedure in the Security Council</item>
                        <label>2.</label>
                        <item>Initial membership</item>
                        <label>3.</label>
                        <item>Location of the United Nations Organization</item>
                        <label>4.</label>
                        <item>Arrangements for International Trusteeships</item>
                        <label>5.</label>
                        <item>Drafting of Court statute</item>
                        <label>6.</label>
                        <item>Procedure for the termination of the League of Nations</item>
                    </list>
                </p>
                <pb facs="0132" n="50" xml:id="pg50"/>
                <p>There are attached hereto recommendations as regards the first four of these
                    questions.</p>
                <p>As regards the Court statute, it was tentatively agreed at Dumbarton Oaks that a
                    group of legal experts would meet two or three weeks prior to the opening of the
                    Conference to draft the document.</p>
                <p>As regards procedure for the termination of the League of Nations, the British
                    and the Chinese governments have appointed committees to work on this subject
                    and have promised to communicate their conclusions to us.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
